# Intake form (deepen facts in the browser)

When Alessandro is giving **durable useful information** about a domain (home, garden,
devices, preferences, projects, people roles, …) and the typed store has **empty
high-value fields** for that domain, offer **once** to open a short browser form.

## Propose (do not open yet)

One short question, for example:
«Sto registrando questi fatti. Posso aprirti un modulo con i campi già detti più quelli
utili ancora vuoti?»

Skip if: trivial turn; he already declined this topic this chat; only secrets/sensitive
would fill the gaps; Cloud/iPhone without Mac (describe fields in chat instead).

## After he agrees (Mac)

1. Build fields: what he already said (**pre-filled**) + important empty fields from the
   matching `system/personal-data/*.md` sheet (or inbox if no sheet fits).
2. Cap about **8–12 fields**. No password, CF, IBAN, clinical health, exact document numbers.
3. Run:

```bash
python3 scripts/intake_form.py open --title "…" --dest "07-giardino-orto-piante.md" \
  --field "Label|prefilled value|hint" \
  --field "Empty useful field||why it helps"
```

4. When saved, confirm path in one line; apply `fact-capture` / `proactive-recall` as usual.

## Efficiency

- At most one form proposal per topic per chat.
- Prefer updating an existing personal-data sheet over a new inbox note.
- Never block the main task waiting on the form; he can fill it while you continue.
